{
  "purpose": "Representative M1 weather input: replaces the single 49N/32E screening point with a wheat-area-weighted national series from 24 oblast points.",
  "retrieved_utc": "2026-11-06",
  "retrieval_route": "NASA POWER Daily API responses were fetched in the project member's desktop browser (the build container cannot reach power.larc.nasa.gov). Daily-to-monthly aggregation and weighting ran on the fetched responses using the algorithm in scripts/fetch_week4_weighted_weather.py. The same browser-side aggregation reproduced the committed single-point snapshot's 264 monthly values byte-for-byte (SHA-256 6f7228a3...0bd6 over month,precip,tmax,tmin,days), so it matches the Week 2 rules. Teammates with internet access can regenerate everything with the script and compare hashes.",
  "api_version": "POWER Daily API v2.10.3 (MERRA-2/POWER sources), AG community, UTC time standard, 2001-01-01 to 2022-12-31; 8,035 daily values per parameter per point; 0 fill values (-999) found.",
  "method": {
    "per_point_monthly": "precipitation_sum_mm = sum of daily PRECTOTCORR (mm/day); t2m_max_mean_c and t2m_min_mean_c = mean of daily T2M_MAX/T2M_MIN; -999 excluded (identical to src/foodshield/etl/week2.py silver_weather_monthly).",
    "national_value": "Weighted mean across the 24 oblast points using fixed weights rounded to 8 decimals; weights renormalised over points with data (all 24 present in every month).",
    "weights": "Mean final-season SSSU wheat harvested area 2015-2020 per oblast divided by the oblast total (6,540.33 thousand ha, equal to the SSSU national total). No 2021-2022 information enters the weights.",
    "points": "Oblast polygon centroid from geoBoundaries gbOpen UKR ADM1 (file SHA-256 b2f9f4ad2e9be5888523219c0bb46a24332ead16b46305409098048fd361a2d6); Odesa uses a representative interior point because its centroid falls outside the polygon."
  },
